---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is Nudgy?",
    a: `Nudgy is a lightweight Mac screenshot tool for capturing, annotating, and sharing visual feedback. Grab any part of your screen, mark it up with arrows, shapes, blur, highlights, and text, then paste it into AI tools, Slack, Jira, GitHub, or wherever work happens.

It's built for speed. One shortcut to capture, a few clicks to annotate, and you're done.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Who is Nudgy for?",
    a: `Nudgy is for vibe coders, product managers, designers, developers, support teams, sales engineers, and anyone in tech who needs to explain what's on screen quickly.

If you've ever spent three paragraphs describing a UI bug you could have just circled, Nudgy is for you.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can I use Nudgy with AI tools?",
    a: `Yes. Nudgy is useful for giving Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and similar tools better visual context. Capture the screenshot, mark what matters, and paste it into your AI workflow.

Annotated screenshots remove ambiguity from prompts. AI models understand images natively — a marked-up screenshot with an arrow pointing at a bug gives far more context than a paragraph trying to describe it.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How is Nudgy different from a normal screenshot?",
    a: `A normal screenshot shows the screen. Nudgy helps you show what matters.

With arrows, circles, highlights, blur, and text labels, you can point attention exactly where it needs to go. The result is a screenshot that actually communicates — not just a raw capture that requires a paragraph of explanation alongside it.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Why not just use built-in macOS screenshots?",
    a: `macOS captures great screenshots. But the moment you need to circle something, draw an arrow, or write "fix this" next to a bug, you're opening Preview or another app and losing your flow.

Nudgy does capture and annotation in one step. Shortcut, select, annotate, paste. You're back in your workflow in seconds, not minutes.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Does anything get uploaded or sent to a server?",
    a: `No. Nudgy runs entirely on your Mac. No cloud, no server, no analytics, no telemetry. Your screenshots never leave your machine unless you explicitly choose to share them.

This matters especially if you're working on proprietary code, internal tools, or client projects. Your visual context stays private.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How fast is the workflow?",
    a: `Under 10 seconds from shortcut to annotated screenshot in your AI tool. And that's if you're taking your time.

The global shortcut triggers from anywhere, so you never leave the app you're working in. Capture, mark up, paste. That's the whole flow.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Is it really free?",
    a: `The core product is free forever. Capture, annotate, save locally — no limits on that for 25 screenshots per month, no account required.

Pro tiers unlock unlimited screenshots, shareable links, animated GIFs, and cloud storage for teams that need more. But the free version is a fully capable tool, not a trial.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="heading">FAQ</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="list">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="item">
          <summary class="question">
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <div class="answer-inner">
              {item.a.split('\n\n').map((para) => (
                <p>{para}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('details.item').forEach(details => {
    const summary = details.querySelector('summary')!;
    const answer = details.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.answer')!;

    summary.addEventListener('click', e => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (details.open) {
        answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + 'px';
        requestAnimationFrame(() => { answer.style.maxHeight = '0'; });
        answer.addEventListener('transitionend', () => { details.open = false; }, { once: true });
      } else {
        details.open = true;
        answer.style.maxHeight = '0';
        requestAnimationFrame(() => { answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + 'px'; });
        answer.addEventListener('transitionend', () => { answer.style.maxHeight = ''; }, { once: true });
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .faq {
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .item {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .question::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .question:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .chevron {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .item[open] .chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .item[open] .question {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .answer {
    overflow: hidden;
    max-height: 0;
    transition: max-height 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .item[open] .answer {
    max-height: 600px;
  }

  .answer-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .answer p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
</style>
